  "changes": [
    "Retain the original pre-call x8 input through LowIR, ABI recovery, source pointer-use analysis, LLVM and both C projections. Keep parameter/result aliases and writes observable during the call; do not copy a logical result back afterward.",
    "Share packet layout, assembly and clobbers in AArch64SourceResultCall.def. Raw BLR and IA/IB authenticated calls preserve their original target and modifier. Only named compiler code addresses are stripped before raw calls.",
    "Use the natural-record PCS classifier for indirect results, including mixed and five-member homogeneous records, without sret/byval/noalias/nonnull/alignment/dereferenceability promises on original storage.",
    "Force a compiler frame, retain its SP in a callee-saved register, reserve aligned outgoing arguments plus the Darwin red zone, and mark assembly as potentially unwinding. C output requires AArch64 Clang with -fexceptions.",
    "Prove complete stack-carried copy-pointer bytes, actual type alignment, initialized private storage, nonoverlap and post-consumption lifetime. Retain taint on unrelated pointer spills; share the same decisions with native-state preservation queries.",
    "Use the existing private-frame read proof during every HighIR DCE phase. Re-run private-store cleanup after final liveness changes so unobserved initializers do not retain unrelocatable image addresses. Unknown memory observers and escapes still refuse cleanup."
  ],
